  "findings": [
    "Native requested output accepts1..512; effective output is min(requested,512\u2212full encoded prompt count). Complete prompt must fit with at least one generation slot; byte truncation is detected by exact byte-count guard.",
    "Native BOS/SentencePiece and English Answer suffix remain profile-specific; EOS2 for learned SentencePiece and70 for byte512. A completed non-EOS output distinguishes contextLimit from tokenLimit.",
    "The generation loop uses actual NativeTinyDecoder final-position logits and unrestricted finite greedy selection, with no oracle/answer inputs. Original weights and tokenizer guards remain intact.",
    "Native explicit MTL device check precedes MLX model evaluation. Its110s internal deadline or120s alarm/controller can still interrupt before a final result; partial token events must not be graded as completed success.",
    "The installed mlx_lm.stream_generate implementation yields each predicted token exactly once: it withholds the last capped/EOS item until the final GenerationResponse. Collecting token and text segment from every response correctly includes final detokenizer flush.",
    "Llama uses original single-user chat template and seed0/temp0; its saved template starts with BOS, so no duplicate BOS is added. Exact input text is preserved, including literal escape characters rather than the earlier CLI escape expansion.",
    "Llama asset hashes are captured before/after. The weights SHA is fixed; final readback must separately join returned sidecar file hashes to the sealed base BUILD manifest.",
    "No extra model runtime/GPU invocation, training, compile, source modification or build-folder modification was performed for this review."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native512 is total context; Llama512 is requested output within its larger context. Same question text is not equal tokenization, equal compute or a standardized benchmark.",
    "GPU/timeout failures are lifecycle outcomes, not wrong model answers. Actual completed evidence remains to be reviewed separately."
  ],
